  ],
  "mach:judgement": "Assess",
  "mach:judgementReason": "A clinician-curated discovery layer that surfaces open healthcare and biomedical datasets across many specialties, run by an active ~5,000-member community of practising clinicians and researchers. Its value is the human curation and the unique items it foregrounds — the HC4 65B-token healthcare pretraining corpus, a ~575,000-patient Synthea synthetic cohort, and MIMIC-IV-Ext clinical time-series sets — alongside pointers to the major open repositories. Marked Assess rather than Adopt for three reasons: it hosts no data and exposes no API or structured, harvestable metadata (it is a curated web page, not a machine-actionable catalog); it asserts no catalog-level licence, with terms varying per linked dataset and governed entirely by the host repositories; and there is no per-dataset licence or quality discipline carried at the archive level. It is best treated as a 'where to find more' starting point for teams building healthcare AI, not as a substitute for direct, evidence-backed dataset entries — datasets it links (e.g. TCIA, PhysioNet collections) should still be cataloged individually where they merit it.",
  "mach:editorialReviewedAt": "2026-06-15",
